# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# Not a style preference. Several files here are *generated* and then compared
# byte-for-byte in CI — `docs/COVERAGE.md` is regenerated by `bishop coverage`
# and checked with `git diff --exit-code` to prove it is current. Without this,
# a file written on Windows lands with CRLF, Linux regenerates it with LF, and
# every one of its lines reads as changed. That is exactly the failure this
# repository hit: a green build on the author's machine and a red one in CI,
# with a diff showing 112 lines replaced by 112 identical lines.
#
# The generators also pass `newline="\n"` explicitly, so their output does not
# depend on the platform in the first place. This file is the backstop for
# everything they do not write.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts must keep CRLF or they will not run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
